# Alkanes - Simple chains (very similar to each other)
C Methane
CC Ethane
CCC Propane
CCCC Butane
CCCCC Pentane
CCCCCC Hexane
CCCCCCC Heptane
CCCCCCCC Octane
CCCCCCCCC Nonane
CCCCCCCCCC Decane

# Branched alkanes - Similar to linear but slightly different
CC(C)C Isobutane
CC(C)CC Isopentane
CC(C)CCC Isohexane
CC(C)(C)C Neopentane
CCC(C)CC 3-Methylpentane
CC(C)C(C)C 2,3-Dimethylbutane

# Benzene derivatives - All very similar (aromatic family)
c1ccccc1 Benzene
Cc1ccccc1 Toluene
CCc1ccccc1 Ethylbenzene
Cc1ccccc1C o-Xylene
Cc1ccc(C)cc1 p-Xylene
Cc1cccc(C)c1 m-Xylene
c1ccccc1C(C)C Cumene
CCCc1ccccc1 Propylbenzene

# Phenols - Similar structure, different substitution
c1ccccc1O Phenol
Cc1ccccc1O o-Cresol
Cc1ccc(O)cc1 p-Cresol
Cc1cccc(O)c1 m-Cresol
Cc1c(O)cccc1C 2,6-Dimethylphenol
CC(C)c1ccc(O)cc1 p-Isopropylphenol

# Anilines - Similar to phenols but with NH2
c1ccccc1N Aniline
Cc1ccccc1N o-Toluidine
Cc1ccc(N)cc1 p-Toluidine
Cc1cccc(N)c1 m-Toluidine
Nc1ccc(N)cc1 p-Phenylenediamine

# Alcohols - Different chain lengths
CO Methanol
CCO Ethanol
CCCO 1-Propanol
CC(C)O 2-Propanol
CCCCO 1-Butanol
CC(C)CO Isobutanol
CC(O)CC 2-Butanol
CCCCCO 1-Pentanol
CCCCCCO 1-Hexanol

# Ketones - Similar functional group
CC(=O)C Acetone
CC(=O)CC 2-Butanone
CCC(=O)CC 3-Pentanone
CC(=O)CCC 2-Pentanone
CC(=O)CCCC 2-Hexanone
CC(=O)c1ccccc1 Acetophenone
CC(=O)c1ccc(C)cc1 p-Methylacetophenone

# Carboxylic acids - Similar to ketones
C(=O)O Formic_acid
CC(=O)O Acetic_acid
CCC(=O)O Propionic_acid
CCCC(=O)O Butyric_acid
CCCCC(=O)O Valeric_acid
c1ccccc1C(=O)O Benzoic_acid
Cc1ccccc1C(=O)O o-Toluic_acid

# Esters - Similar to acids
CC(=O)OC Methyl_acetate
CCOC(=O)C Ethyl_acetate
CC(=O)OCC Ethyl_acetate_alt
CCCOC(=O)C Propyl_acetate
CC(=O)OCCC Propyl_acetate_alt

# Ethers - Oxygen bridge
COC Dimethyl_ether
CCOC Ethyl_methyl_ether
CCOCC Diethyl_ether
c1ccccc1OC Anisole
c1ccccc1OCc2ccccc2 Benzyl_phenyl_ether

# Nitriles
C#N Hydrogen_cyanide
CC#N Acetonitrile
CCC#N Propionitrile
c1ccccc1C#N Benzonitrile
Cc1ccccc1C#N o-Tolunitrile

# Polycyclic aromatics - Very similar to each other
c1ccc2ccccc2c1 Naphthalene
c1ccc2c(c1)ccc1ccccc12 Anthracene
c1ccc2c(c1)ccc1c2cccc1 Phenanthrene
c1ccc2cc3ccccc3cc2c1 Pyrene

# Heterocycles - 5-membered rings (similar family)
c1ccoc1 Furan
c1ccsc1 Thiophene
c1cc[nH]c1 Pyrrole
Cc1ccoc1 2-Methylfuran
c1csc(C)c1 2-Methylthiophene

# Heterocycles - 6-membered rings (similar family)
c1ccncc1 Pyridine
c1cnccc1 Pyridine_isomer
Cc1ccncc1 2-Methylpyridine
Cc1cccnc1 3-Methylpyridine
Cc1ccnc(C)c1 2,6-Dimethylpyridine
c1ccnc2ccccc12 Quinoline
c1ccc2ncccc2c1 Isoquinoline

# Halogenated aromatics - Similar base structures
c1ccccc1F Fluorobenzene
c1ccccc1Cl Chlorobenzene
c1ccccc1Br Bromobenzene
c1ccccc1I Iodobenzene
Fc1ccccc1F o-Difluorobenzene
Fc1ccc(F)cc1 p-Difluorobenzene

# Nitro compounds
c1ccccc1[N+](=O)[O-] Nitrobenzene
Cc1ccccc1[N+](=O)[O-] o-Nitrotoluene
Cc1ccc([N+](=O)[O-])cc1 p-Nitrotoluene

# Amino acids (simplified)
NCC(=O)O Glycine
CC(N)C(=O)O Alanine
CC(C)C(N)C(=O)O Valine
CCC(N)C(=O)O 2-Aminobutyric_acid

# Drug-like molecules
CC(C)Cc1ccc(cc1)C(C)C(=O)O Ibuprofen
CC(=O)Oc1ccccc1C(=O)O Aspirin
CC(C)NCC(O)c1ccc(O)c(O)c1 Isoproterenol
Cc1ccc(cc1)S(=O)(=O)N Toluenesulfonamide

# Sugars (open chain)
OCC(O)C(O)C(O)C(O)C=O Glucose_linear
OCC(O)C(O)C(O)C=O Erythrose

# Terpenes
CC(=C)C1CCC(=C)CC1 Limonene
CC(C)=CCCC(C)=C Myrcene
CC1=CCC(CC1)C(=C)C alpha-Terpinene

# Cycloalkanes
C1CCCC1 Cyclopentane
C1CCCCC1 Cyclohexane
C1CCCCCC1 Cycloheptane
C1CCC(C)CC1 Methylcyclohexane

# Bicyclic compounds
C1CC2CCC1C2 Norbornane
C1CCC2CCCCC2C1 Decalin

# Miscellaneous
O Water
N Ammonia
S Hydrogen_sulfide
c1ccc2c(c1)OCO2 Benzodioxole
CC1(C)CCCC(C)(C)O1 Musk_ketone
